    "title": "'Survivor 50' contestant from Jersey facing antisemitism allegations",
    "text": "March 2, 2026Updated March 3, 2026, 7:04 a.m. ET“Survivor 50” contestant Stephenie LaGrossa Kendrick of Toms River is making news away from the island.Kendrick was called out in the summer of 2025 for being a supporter of President Donald Trump by a fellow “Survivor” alum and she responded with antisemitic language. The controversy over Kendrick's language is bubbling up again as the premiere of “Survivor 50” on Wednesday, Feb. 25 was a ratings hit with more than five million viewers.Fellow “Survivor” alum Eliza Orlins wrote a Substack article called “The Stephenie LaGrossa Kendrick Files: MAGA, Misinformation, and Deleted Receipts” in May of 2025.“Eliza tried to bury me about Donald Trump and I'm going to tell you something right now, that's bull (blank),” said Kendrick in social media video that was captured by Orlins and can be seen on Orlins' social media, but watch the language. “Don't come at me with your political status when you're (blanking) Jewish and your parents are one percent of the population of wealth.”Kendrick reposted an apology originally posted in August 2025 on the eve of the “Survivor 50” debut last week.“During a conversation in which I was calling out someone for what I perceived as a lack of support for the Jewish community, I misspoke in a way that was abrupt, poorly worded, and offensive,” Kendrick said. “What I meant to express was frustration that someone who is Jewish was not standing up for their own community in a moment that called for unity and support. However, the way I said it was wrong and I take full responsibility for how it came across.”Kendrick, married to former Philadelphia Phillies pitcher Kyle Kendrick with three children, previously appeared on “Survivor: Palau,” “Survivor: Guatemala,” “Survivor: Heroes vs. Villains,” and “The Traitors.” She lives in Tampa Bay with her family.Orlins, a former contestant on “Survivor” and “Amazing Race,” is a New York City public defender and former candidate for Manhattan District Attorney. She's been critical of the perceived political leaning CBS has taken since Trump donor supporter David Ellison acquired CBS's parent company, Paramount Global.“This story broke and was covered widely and CBS's response was not to speak out about how unacceptable this was, but to continue to prop her up,” said Orlins on social media. “But this isn't just about me, and this isn't just about 'Survivor.' CBS has spent the last year making a series of choices that tell you exactly who they are and what they value.”“Survivor 50” was filmed in Fiji. A request for comment from “Survivor” producers and Kendrick submitted to CBS Entertainment was not responded to by press time.Subscribe to app.com for the latest on New Jersey celebs.Chris Jordan, a Jersey Shore native, covers entertainment and features for the USA Today Network New Jersey. Contact him at cjordan@app.com",
